## Fix: Task 6 review round 1 (matching base runs, bounded change feed, shared helpers)
================================================================================

Context: Review round 1 of Task 6 found three Important and twelve Minor
items. The net change apply and the MERGE skip could continue from a base run
whose `_data` history had restarted (MV <-> MERGE table), the MERGE skip could
fire on a store dropped outside a build or never on the Delta engine, a change
feed lost half-way failed the build, and the window read by the count and the
stream was open-ended. The run-history methods left TwinBuildPostMaterialize
for their own class, and several copies were consolidated.

Changes:

1. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/TwinBuildRunHistory.py (new, re-exported)
   Extract Class from TwinBuildPostMaterialize: `build_run_stats`,
   `build_run_key`, `store_identity`, `previous_materialization_stats`, the
   base-run search and `strategy` (now public); every caller updated, no shim.
   Base search over 50 runs (was 10); `apply_mode == "none"` is a base when the
   current backend is the Delta engine; a success of the same graph in another
   sync mode ends the search. New `data_table_id` fact and
   `completion_summary(pipe)` (label and build_mode from apply_mode and the
   effective mode).
2. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/TwinBuildPostMaterialize.py
   Back to 269 lines; `text_attr` is the shared string-attribute reader.
3. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/TwinNetChangeApply.py
   `applies` also needs an `mv` / `merge` `_data`. The base must have the same
   strategy and, when both runs know it, the same table id (`DESCRIBE
   DETAIL`); otherwise `no_previous_version`. The window `(since, latest]` is
   passed to the count and the stream. A change-feed error raised while the
   net changes are written (tagged apart from store write errors) falls back to
   the full stream with `cdf_unavailable`. The extra adjacency rebuild after
   the purge is gone (the purge rebuilds the graph cache).
4. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/TwinMergeFallback.py
   The fingerprint skip also needs `_data` at the base's recorded version and,
   off the Delta engine, `store.table_exists(graph)` when the store has it.
   The skipped build completes through `_BuildPipeline._complete_task`.
5. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/_build_pipeline.py
   `_complete_task(*, message="", build_mode="")`: defaults from
   `completion_summary` ("Net change apply" / "Incremental build" / "Full
   rebuild"; build_mode incremental unless the mode is full or the store was
   fully streamed). New `data_table_id` attribute.
6. src/back/core/graphdb/delta/ChangeFeedReader.py
   `net_changes_sql` / `iter_net_changes` / `changeset_ratio` take
   `until_version` and read `table_changes('<fqn>', since + 1, until)`; new
   `table_id` (best-effort `DESCRIBE DETAIL` id).
7. src/back/core/helpers/WarehouseStatements.py (new, re-exported from
   back.core.helpers), src/back/core/streaming/SourceReadiness.py
   One name guard and one driver-error translation for ChangeFeedReader and
   SourceReadiness (the copies are removed).
8. src/back/core/graphdb/delta/materialize.py,
   src/back/core/graphdb/delta/DeltaMergeMaterializer.py,
   src/back/core/helpers/SQLHelpers.py,
   src/back/core/graphdb/delta/MaterializedViewBuilder.py,
   src/back/core/graphdb/lakebase/_companion_ddl.py
   `materialize.CHANGE_FEED_PROPERTIES` extends the row-tracking properties for
   the MERGE table; `SQLHelpers.object_hash_sql` is the one `sha2(…, 256)`
   expression of the MV, the wrapped VIEW and the MERGE (SQL output unchanged).
9. src/back/core/graphdb/lakebase/LakebaseFlatStore.py
   `_drain_batches` raises ValidationError for a batch size below 1 (class at
   1153 lines, a docstring line trimmed).
10. Tests: tests/units/graphdb/delta/test_change_feed_reader.py (bounded
    window, table id), tests/units/core/test_warehouse_statements.py (new),
    tests/units/core/test_lakebase_flat_store.py (batch size),
    tests/units/objects/test_build_pipeline_net_apply.py (Delta-engine skip,
    strategy and table-id mismatch, dropped store, base version moved,
    half-read feed, completion messages, sync-mode switch, CTAS / view not
    applicable, single cache rebuild, 50-run window).

Known limitations (deferred by review):
- An existing MERGE table without `object_hash` (a domain that became
  Lakeflow-synced) fails its first hashed MERGE, which falls back to the CTAS.
- Every MERGE build re-applies the table properties (one metadata commit).
- With no new `_data` version the net apply still purges, optimizes and
  rebuilds the graph cache.
- Neo4j always streams in full (`inferred_not_separable`).

