## Fix: Task 8 review round 1 (reconciler counts like the MV, honest 404, DAB template)
================================================================================

Context: the Task 8 review found the reconciler reporting drift on healthy
graphs, a 404 that also covered outages, and a DAB template that did not match
the runner.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/helpers/SQLHelpers.py, src/back/core/graphdb/delta/MaterializedViewBuilder.py,
   src/back/core/streaming/SlotReconciler.py
   `NON_BLANK_OBJECT_SQL` (the `WHERE object IS NOT NULL AND TRIM(object) != ''`
   the `_data` MV applies to its slots branch) is now one constant; the
   reconciler applies it inside both DISTINCT totals and the per-`map_id`
   query, so `_slots` rows for unset attributes (blank objects kept as
   upserts) no longer read as drift. An unreadable count or a missing row is
   an `InfrastructureError`, not a zero (two garbled answers must not compare
   equal). Comment on the DECIMAL(38,0) cast made exact (BIGINT sums overflow
   after a handful of 64-bit hashes in ANSI mode).
2. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/TwinSlotReconciliation.py
   A missing warehouse client is an `InfrastructureError`; the slots table is
