## Incremental triple materialization — roll-up (Tasks 0-8)
================================================================================

Context (branch state): `origin/master` (the default branch) had no commits beyond
the merge base b3f70b9a after `git fetch --all`; the release line `origin/0.9.2`
(version 0.9.2, six fixes) is merged into the branch (a3481562), which is why these
changelog files live under v0.9.2 and the README gained a "What's new in 0.9.2"
section. The design document was re-read against the branch; the traceability
table is in docs/incremental-materialization.md ("Design traceability").

Context: per-domain materialization modes `full` / `incremental` / `microbatch`
(`realtime` reserved) for the knowledge-graph build, implemented over
2026-11-01 (Tasks 0-5, 7: changelogs/v0.9.1/dermot-smyth_2026-11-01.log) and
2026-11-02 (Tasks 6, 8: this file). Design: docs/incremental-materialization.md.

1. Task 0 — compute the mapped triples once (`_data` is the counted, streamed
   and synced source) and reset `_inferred` in the main build.
2. Task 1 — per-domain `materialization_mode` setting, `ModeDecision`,
   `MaterializationModeResolver` (fallback ladder), UI surfacing.
3. Task 2 — `SlotProjectionCompiler`: row-local mappings to Lakeflow slot-event
   SQL and `AUTO CDC … SCD TYPE 1` flows; `SourceReadiness` probes.
4. Task 3 — translator incremental mode (`TripleSQLAssembler`) and
   `MaterializedViewBuilder` (`_data` MV, `REFRESH POLICY INCREMENTAL`).
5. Task 4 — `SlotPipelineRunner` + `TwinIncrementalBuild`: the
   incremental / microbatch build path with fallbacks, fingerprints and MV reuse.
6. Task 5 — Lakebase sync follows the mode (`TwinLakebaseSync`, `SyncPlan`,
   continuous wait, drift handling); scheduled builds probe like the main build.
7. Task 6 — `ChangeFeedReader`, `DeltaMergeMaterializer`, `TwinNetChangeApply`
   (net changes into Neo4j / app-managed Lakebase), `TwinMergeFallback` (MERGE
   without serverless, fingerprint skip), `TwinBuildRunHistory`
   (`stats.materialization`, base-run selection).
8. Task 7 — Lakehouse//RT read routing for the Delta engine with a reads-only
   fallback that keeps the caller's identity.
9. Task 8 — `SlotReconciler` + `POST /dtwin/incremental/reconcile`, the docs
   guide, the DAB template and the cockpit badge.

Final test result (after the design-gaps review fixes): 10764 passed, 339 skipped, 9 deselected
(`uv run --frozen pytest -q -m "not scenario"` with the readiness-route test
deselected); architecture suite green; `tests/units/architecture/baseline.json`
unchanged.

