- The `view_data` and `sync_data` pairs compare as of the last refresh of
  `_data`: a source changed since shows as drift until the next build or tick
  (the tick reconciles right after its refresh, so its window is the tick
  itself).
- Neo4j net apply: see item 7.
- TwinIncrementalStatus reads the synced-table state through
  `SyncedTableManager._extract_state` / `_extract_status_message`, as
  GraphEngineLakebaseSettings already does (the class is at its frozen size
  budget, so no public wrapper was added).

